# Grok Build CLI (Town of Wiley)

Full reference: [`docs/grok-cli.md`](../../docs/grok-cli.md). Project rules: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

## Auth model (do not deviate)

- **Heavy only:** OAuth + `grok-build` via `grok login --oauth` (SuperGrok / X Premium+).
- **Never** export `XAI_API_KEY` or `GROK_CODE_XAI_API_KEY` in the shell for this workflow — they override OAuth.
- `~/.zshrc` defines a `grok()` wrapper that unsets API-key env vars and defaults `-m grok-build`.

## Shell setup (Cursor / agent terminals)

Non-interactive shells may not load `~/.zshrc`. Prefix Grok commands:

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.grok/bin:$PATH"
source ~/.zshrc   # optional; loads grok() wrapper
```

Node 24 for npm in this repo (separate from Grok):

```bash
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH"   # macOS Homebrew; Intel: /usr/local/opt/node@24/bin
```

## Health check (run before blaming auth)

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.grok/bin:$PATH"
source ~/.zshrc
grok --version
grok models          # expect: logged in with grok.com, default grok-build
grok -p "reply with exactly: ok"
grok mcp doctor
```

- `Auth(AuthorizationRequired)` in logs **while `-p` still prints a response** is a known headless worker quirk — not missing API key. Refresh with `grok login --oauth` or use interactive `grok` (no `-p`).
- If `grok: command not found`, PATH is wrong — use exports above.

## Canonical commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Interactive session | `grok` |
| Headless one-shot | `grok -p "prompt"` |
| Auto-approve tools (headless) | `grok -p "prompt" --yolo` or `--always-approve` |
| Wrong (parsed as `-y`) | ~~`-yolo`~~, ~~`-y`~~ |
| Project + MCP inspect | `grok inspect` |
| Refresh OAuth | `grok login --oauth` |
| MCP diagnostics | `grok mcp doctor` |

## CI / GitHub Actions (prefer `gh`, not Grok fetch)

Do **not** ask Grok to fetch GitHub Actions URLs. Use `gh`:

```bash
gh run list --limit 5
gh run view <run-id> --log-failed
gh pr checks <number>
```

Fix failures with repo scripts: `npm run lint`, `npm run test:unit:browser`, `npm run test:e2e:smoke`, `trunk check --fix`.

## MCP (Grok vs Cursor)

Project MCP: [`.grok/config.toml`](../../.grok/config.toml) (mirrors [`.cursor/mcp.json`](../../.cursor/mcp.json)).

| Server | Grok notes |
|--------|------------|
| angular-cli, playwright-test, github, mermaid | Usually healthy |
| playwright-mcp | Use `@playwright/mcp@latest` (not `@1.59.1` — version does not exist on npm) |
| figma | Separate OAuth from `grok login`; authenticate in Grok TUI when prompted |
| primeng | Often broken upstream (MCP SDK/Zod); prefer angular-cli + PrimeNG docs |

## Trunk / script encoding

If Trunk reports `invalid UTF-8` or shellcheck SC1072 on `scripts/configure-cloudfront-weather-cache.sh` or `scripts/deploy-contact-updates-review.py`, restore from git:

```bash
git checkout HEAD -- scripts/configure-cloudfront-weather-cache.sh scripts/deploy-contact-updates-review.py
```

Avoid smart quotes / mojibake in shell scripts — use ASCII `->` and `-`.
